  <!-- Main Content -->
  <section class=" container content-section">
    <div class="card-overview w-100">
     

      <h2>Ophthalmology</h2>
      <hr>
<div id="ViEtDeVdIvId" style="POSITION:Relative;FONT-FAMILY:Arial;FONT-SIZE:12px; BACKGROUND-COLOR:white"><div style=""><p style="line-height: 107%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; margin-left: 0in; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; word-break: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" face="Verdana" size="2">The Eye Department of NRCH is well equipped, and providing world class services available in house. </font></p> <p style="line-height: 107%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; margin-left: 0in; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; word-break: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" face="Verdana" size="2">Four UPSC qualified regular doctors are present in the department.&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(0, 176, 80);">Dr. Amita Jain </span>with more than 30 years’ experience, <span style="color: rgb(0, 176, 80);">Dr. S.K. Choudhary </span>with more than 20 years’ experience, <span style="color: rgb(0, 176, 80);">Dr. Saloni Gupta </span>and<span style="color: rgb(0, 176, 80);">Dr. Rishi Sethi</span>, both with more than 10 years’ experience.&nbsp;</font><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">All four eye specialists are providing very high-quality patient care with the latest techniques and medicines, and performing hundreds of major surgeries individually with extremely satisfying results.</span></p><p style="line-height: 107%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; margin-left: 0in; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; word-break: normal;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;"><img src="https://nr.indianrailways.gov.in//uploads/images/1761041253024-Picture11.png"><br></span></p> <p style="line-height: 107%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; margin-left: 0in; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; word-break: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" face="Verdana" size="2">Dr. Saloni Gupta and Dr. Rishi Sethi are AIIMS-trained specialists in corneal diseases and glaucoma, respectively.&nbsp;</font><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" face="Verdana" size="2">Apart from these four regular doctors, four senior resident doctors, and eight DNB student doctors are also present in the department.&nbsp;</font><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">All the doctors are very courteous and caring, and are available round the clock in the hospital for eye emergency services.</span></p><p style="line-height: 107%; margin: 0pt 0in 8pt; text-indent: 0in; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; word-break: normal;"><span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; letter-spacing: 0pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" face="Verdana" size="2">Both senior and junior doctors keep themselves updated by attending national and international seminars and conferences. They also share experiences and research work with national and international faculties.</font></span></p><p style="line-height: 107%; margin: 0pt 0in 8pt; text-indent: 0in; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; word-break: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" face="Verdana" size="2"><span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; letter-spacing: 0pt; vertical-align: baseline;">The retina disorder management is also of American standards with all the latest </span><span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; letter-spacing: 0pt; vertical-align: baseline;">equipments</span><span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; letter-spacing: 0pt; vertical-align: baseline;">and medications. The common retinal disorders are Diabetic retinopathy, Age related Macular degeneration, Retinal Venous conclusion and&nbsp;</span></font><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small; letter-spacing: 0pt; text-indent: 0in;">Central serous retinopathy. For diagnosis of these retinal disorders, we have fundus fluorescence angiography, OCT angiography and eye ultrasound, and to treat these disorders we have medicines and lasers.</span></p><p style="line-height: 107%; margin: 0pt 0in 8pt; text-indent: 0in; text-align: left; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; word-break: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" face="Verdana" size="2"><span style="font-variant: normal; color: black; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-style: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">We also have the latest intravitreal injections to treat progressive retinal disorders. Foradvanced retinal </span><span style="font-variant: normal; color: black; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-style: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">disorders, we</span><span style="font-variant: normal; color: black; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-style: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">have the latest vitrectomy machine and a Carl Zeiss retinal microscope.</span></font></p></div><div style="font-size: 12px; font-family: Arial;"><br></div><div style="font-size: 12px; font-family: Arial;"><br></div><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" face="Arial"><img src="https://nr.indianrailways.gov.in//uploads/images/1731923188919-Ophthalmology Schedule.png"></font><br></div>    
</div>
